# Git Installation & Essential Commands

## Install Git

```bash
apt install git-all -y
```

## Check Git Version

```bash
git --version
```

---

# Repository Setup

## Initialize a New Repository

```bash
git init
```

## Check Repository Status

```bash
git status
```

---

# Staging Files

## Add a Specific File

```bash
git add <filename>
```

## Add All Files

```bash
git add .
```

## Remove a File from the Staging Area

```bash
git rm --cached <filename>
```

---

# Commit Changes

## Create a Commit

```bash
git commit -m "Your commit message"
```

---

# Remote Repository

## Push Code to Remote Repository

```bash
git push origin main
```

---

# View Commit History

## Detailed Commit Log

```bash
git log
```

## Compact One-Line Log

```bash
git log --oneline
```
